@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] protocol-pure-shared-boundary
The shared protocol library MUST remain independent of Ash, database access and
durable credential storage. Versioned codecs, state machines, Cadence and the
single-writer View MUST remain free of socket/filesystem I/O (ADR-0012/0140).
ADR-0142 permits outbound WebSocket socket I/O only through
OverallsProtocol.WebSocket.Connection and OverallsProtocol.Control.Client;
credential callbacks and configured TLS trust are supplied by the application.
Those transport modules MUST NOT perform host mutations, domain authorization
or credential persistence. Marshall and Lilly remain independent production
applications consuming shared types and transport.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] protocol-peer-values-never-create-atoms
Decoding peer-controlled fields MUST NOT create atoms from peer strings; accepted keys
and enum atoms must come from a finite schema owned by the library.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol] protocol-explicit-version-compatibility
Provisioner v4 is the only supported execution control version under ADR-0037/0149.
Every envelope MUST reject unsupported versions, never reinterpret them. Commands
and outcomes MUST bind placement and execution epoch. Relocation descriptors MUST
NOT grant execution authority. Credential format versions remain
independent. Contract changes require coordinated consumer tests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:assumption] protocol-encoders-require-validated-values
Callers of encode functions MUST supply values already validated against the matching
schema or constructed from trusted typed application state. Encoding alone MUST NOT be
used as evidence that untrusted data is valid.
